# GENERATED from scripts/agent-guard/rules.json by `pnpm guard:generate`; do not edit by hand.
# `pnpm guard:check` fails when this file and rules.json disagree.
#
# Codex execpolicy matches an exact argv prefix: the first words of a command, in order. It
# cannot express what the shared guard core matches by regex, by path or by context, so the
# PreToolUse hook in .codex/hooks.json (the same core Claude Code runs) covers, for every rule:
# - a word after an option or further on (`vercel --cwd x deploy`, `git push -u origin main`);
# - commands inside `sh -c` scripts Codex does not split, `eval`, `xargs`, aliases or quotes;
# - the current branch (`git push` while on main) and which migrations are already committed;
# - the files a branch changes against origin/main (a push that leaves AGENTS.md behind);
# - file edits through apply_patch and shell writes (rm, mv, sed -i, redirects).
# Rules the hook alone enforces in part or in full:
# - no prefix at all: agents-md-current, guardrail-files, management-api, committed-migrations, deploy-config
# - matched by regex: supabase-linked-write, psql-remote, gh-actions-api, gh-api-write, management-api, supabase-link, prod-secrets
# - matched by path: guardrail-files, prod-secrets, committed-migrations, deploy-config
# - matched by environment variable: vercel-credentials, git-hooks-off
# A "prompt" rule is coarser here than in the core, so Codex asks instead of forbidding.

prefix_rule(
    pattern = [["vercel", "vc"], ["login", "logout", "--token", "-t", "switch"]],
    decision = "forbidden",
    justification = "Esto es parte de las buenas prácticas del proyecto para salvaguardar el flujo de desarrollo: este comando cambia o usa credenciales de Vercel desde la terminal. El camino correcto: abrir un PR contra `main`; producción se despliega sola desde `main` una vez revisado y mergeado.\nProject good practice, to keep the development flow safe: this command changes or uses Vercel credentials from the terminal. Correct path: open a PR to `main`; production deploys from `main` once it is reviewed and merged.",
